WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.808
Pronouns: Agreement and Case

00:00:03.188 --> 00:00:05.115
Trace the pronoun back to its noun.

00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:07.314
How to spot it

00:00:07.714 --> 00:00:10.134
Choices like it, its, they, their

00:00:10.684 --> 00:00:12.675
The noun is far back in the sentence

00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:17.040
It’s testing: whether a pronoun matches what it replaces

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.035
The method

00:00:19.435 --> 00:00:22.229
Step 1: Find the noun it replaces

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:24.872
Trace it back, even past commas.

00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:27.383
Step 2: One or many?

00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:29.400
Organisations count as one.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.887
Step 3: Pick the match

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:35.450
One: it, its. Many: they, their.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.908
Step 4: Check the form

00:00:38.188 --> 00:00:40.344
its vs it’s, who vs whom.

00:00:40.894 --> 00:00:42.004
In a few words

00:00:42.154 --> 00:00:44.490
Trace it. Count it. Match it.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.513
The rules

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.679
Organisations take it / its

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:51.667
Wrong: The museum changed their hours.

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:54.437
Right: The museum changed its hours.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.391
Plurals take they / their

00:00:56.671 --> 00:00:59.040
Right: The temples lost their paint.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.344
its = belongs to it, it’s = it is

00:01:02.624 --> 00:01:05.001
Wrong: The town and it’s festival

00:01:05.281 --> 00:01:07.568
Right: The town and its festival

00:01:08.118 --> 00:01:10.089
who = he, whom = him

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.381
Right: the archaeologist whom the team credited

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:17.334
After to, for, with: me, him, them

00:01:17.614 --> 00:01:19.395
Wrong: to Priya and I

00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:21.399
Right: to Priya and me

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:23.639
Let’s try one

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:32.342
The orchestra, founded by a group of retired teachers in 1987, will celebrate ______ fortieth anniversary

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.804
next year with a series of free concerts.

00:01:35.454 --> 00:01:37.243
Skip the part between the commas.

00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:42.539
Who’s celebrating? The orchestra. One group, so it’s singular.

00:01:43.095 --> 00:01:45.515
Their is plural. It’s means it is.

00:01:45.515 --> 00:01:49.950
They’re means they are. Its is singular and shows ownership.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:50.774
Choice B.

00:01:51.974 --> 00:01:52.969
Common traps

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:54.558
The plural decoy

00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:57.759
A plural noun nearby that isn’t the antecedent.

00:01:58.309 --> 00:01:59.989
Organisations as “they”

00:02:00.269 --> 00:02:03.250
Fine when talking. Wrong on the SAT.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.658
Pronouns: Agreement and Case

00:02:06.938 --> 00:02:09.274
Trace it. Count it. Match it.

00:02:09.824 --> 00:02:10.597
Spot it

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.245
it / its / they / their in the choices

00:02:13.795 --> 00:02:14.503
Steps

00:02:14.703 --> 00:02:17.278
1. Trace the pronoun back to its noun

00:02:17.558 --> 00:02:19.944
2. Count it: one or many?

00:02:20.224 --> 00:02:24.055
3. One → it / its; many → they / their

00:02:24.335 --> 00:02:27.898
4. Check the form: its / it’s, who / whom

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.200
Remember

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.680
Companies, teams → it / its

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.045
its = belongs to it; it’s = it is

00:02:35.325 --> 00:02:37.477
who = he; whom = him

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.135
After to / for / with → me, him, them

00:02:41.685 --> 00:02:42.290
Trap

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:44.397
A plural noun planted nearby

00:02:45.147 --> 00:02:48.841
